WEBVTT

00:00.317 --> 00:02.199
- [Voiceover] So we have a
nice, little equation here

00:02.199 --> 00:04.451
that has some rational expressions in it

00:04.451 --> 00:06.033
and like always, pause the video

00:06.033 --> 00:07.497
and see if you can figure out

00:07.497 --> 00:10.720
which x's satisfy this equation.

00:10.720 --> 00:12.105
All right. Let's work through it together.

00:12.105 --> 00:15.448
Now, when I see things at
the denominator like this,

00:15.448 --> 00:18.768
my instinct is to try to not
have denominators like this.

00:18.768 --> 00:21.811
And so what we could do is to
get rid of this x minus one

00:21.811 --> 00:23.243
in the denominator on the left-hand side.

00:23.243 --> 00:25.909
We can multiply both sides of the equation

00:25.909 --> 00:28.324
times x minus one,

00:28.324 --> 00:30.009
x minus one.

00:30.009 --> 00:33.977
We're gonna multiply both
sides by x minus one.

00:33.977 --> 00:37.140
And once again, the
whole point of doing that

00:37.140 --> 00:38.952
is so that we get rid of this x minus one

00:38.952 --> 00:40.854
in the denominator right over here.

00:40.854 --> 00:42.996
And then to get rid of this x plus one

00:42.996 --> 00:44.911
in the denominator over here,

00:44.911 --> 00:49.308
we can multiply both sides of
the equation times x plus one.

00:49.308 --> 00:53.026
So, x plus one.

00:53.026 --> 00:56.156
Multiply both sides times x plus one.

00:56.156 --> 00:58.945
And so what is that going to give us?

00:58.945 --> 01:03.163
Well, on the left-hand
side, that is going to,

01:03.163 --> 01:06.229
x minus one divided by x
minus one is just gonna be one

01:06.229 --> 01:09.781
for the x's where that's defined,

01:09.781 --> 01:11.967
for x not being equal to one.

01:11.967 --> 01:13.620
And so, we're gonna have x plus one

01:13.620 --> 01:15.425
times negative two x plus four.

01:15.425 --> 01:16.770
So let me write that down.

01:16.770 --> 01:19.282
So we have x plus,

01:19.282 --> 01:20.413
I'm gonna need some space,

01:20.413 --> 01:22.569
so let me make sure I don't write too big.

01:22.569 --> 01:26.924
x plus one times negative two x,

01:26.924 --> 01:29.796
negative two x plus four

01:29.796 --> 01:31.778
is going to be equal to.

01:31.778 --> 01:34.404
Now, if we multiply both of these

01:34.404 --> 01:36.950
times three over x plus one,

01:36.950 --> 01:39.339
the x plus one is going to
cancel with the x plus one

01:39.339 --> 01:42.805
and we're gonna be left with
three times x minus one.

01:42.805 --> 01:46.005
So that is going to be
three x minus three,

01:46.005 --> 01:48.514
three x minus three,

01:48.514 --> 01:51.845
and then minus,

01:51.845 --> 01:55.698
minus one times both of these.

01:55.698 --> 01:59.409
So one times x minus one times x plus one.

01:59.409 --> 02:02.278
So, minus one times

02:02.278 --> 02:05.508
x minus one times x plus one.

02:05.508 --> 02:06.706
All I did is I multiplied,

02:06.706 --> 02:08.268
took the x minus one times x plus one,

02:08.268 --> 02:10.440
multiplied times each of these terms.

02:10.440 --> 02:12.392
When I multiply it times this first term,

02:12.392 --> 02:14.584
the x plus one and the
x plus one canceled,

02:14.584 --> 02:17.557
so I just have to multiply
three times x minus one.

02:17.557 --> 02:18.782
And then for the second term,

02:18.782 --> 02:20.814
I just multiply times both of these.

02:20.814 --> 02:22.265
And now you might recognize,

02:22.265 --> 02:25.428
if you have something x
plus one times x minus one,

02:25.428 --> 02:28.281
that's going to be x squared minus one.

02:28.281 --> 02:30.917
So I could rewrite all
of this right over here

02:30.917 --> 02:33.782
as being equal to...

02:33.782 --> 02:36.712
as being equal to

02:36.712 --> 02:38.822
x squared minus one,

02:38.822 --> 02:41.215
and once again, that's
because this is the same thing

02:41.215 --> 02:43.663
as x squared minus one.

02:43.663 --> 02:46.506
And since I'm subtracting
an x squared minus one,

02:46.506 --> 02:49.802
actually, let me just, I don't
wanna do too much on one step

02:49.802 --> 02:51.271
so let's go to the next step.

02:51.271 --> 02:53.807
So, I could multiply this out.

02:53.807 --> 02:58.281
So I could multiply x times negative two x

02:58.281 --> 03:01.224
which would give us
negative two x squared.

03:01.224 --> 03:03.503
x times four,

03:03.503 --> 03:07.143
which is going to give us plus four x

03:07.143 --> 03:09.542
and I could multiply one
times negative two x.

03:09.542 --> 03:11.494
I'm gonna subtract two x.

03:11.494 --> 03:15.755
And then one times four,
which is gonna be plus four,

03:15.755 --> 03:18.445
and then that is going to be equal to,

03:18.445 --> 03:20.433
that is going to be equal to,

03:20.433 --> 03:24.511
we have three x minus three

03:24.511 --> 03:26.293
and then we can distribute
this negative sign.

03:26.293 --> 03:30.453
So we can say minus x squared plus one.

03:30.453 --> 03:32.926
And over here, we can
simplify it a little bit.

03:32.926 --> 03:37.497
This is going to be, that
is four x minus two x

03:37.497 --> 03:39.598
is going to be,

03:39.598 --> 03:40.960
I'm gonna try to write over, yep,

03:40.960 --> 03:43.823
four x minus two x, so
that would be two x.

03:43.823 --> 03:47.594
And so this is simplified to, let's see,

03:47.594 --> 03:49.446
well this is, we have a
negative three and a one,

03:49.446 --> 03:52.799
so those two together
are going to be equal to,

03:52.799 --> 03:54.423
subtracting at two.

03:54.423 --> 03:56.469
So we can rewrite everything as,

03:56.469 --> 03:58.434
do the neutral color now,

03:58.434 --> 04:01.170
negative two x squared

04:01.170 --> 04:04.170
plus two x plus four

04:04.170 --> 04:08.475
is equal to negative x squared

04:08.475 --> 04:12.899
plus three x minus two.

04:12.899 --> 04:15.755
Now we can try to get all of this business

04:15.755 --> 04:17.540
onto the right-hand side,

04:17.540 --> 04:19.172
so let's subtract it from both sides.

04:19.172 --> 04:20.083
So we're gonna subtract,

04:20.083 --> 04:23.605
or we'll say we'll add
x squared to both sides,

04:23.605 --> 04:25.150
add x squared,

04:25.150 --> 04:28.780
that gets rid of this
white negative x squared.

04:28.780 --> 04:31.002
We subtract three x from both sides,

04:31.002 --> 04:33.224
subtract three x from both sides,

04:33.224 --> 04:36.112
add two to both sides, add two,

04:36.112 --> 04:38.945
and we will be left with,

04:38.945 --> 04:41.591
we are going to end up with.

04:41.591 --> 04:43.503
See, negative two x squared plus x squared

04:43.503 --> 04:46.015
is negative x squared.

04:46.015 --> 04:48.608
Two x minus three x is negative x.

04:48.608 --> 04:52.095
And then four plus two is six,

04:52.095 --> 04:53.583
is going to be equal to,

04:53.583 --> 04:56.436
well that's going to
cancel that, that, that,

04:56.436 --> 04:58.138
is equal to zero.

04:58.138 --> 05:00.000
I don't like having this
negative on the x squared,

05:00.000 --> 05:02.842
so let's multiply both
sides times negative one.

05:02.842 --> 05:04.197
And so if I do that,

05:04.197 --> 05:08.087
so if I just take the
negative on both sides,

05:08.087 --> 05:10.513
so I just multiply that
times negative one.

05:10.513 --> 05:12.605
Same thing, it's taking
the negative on both sides.

05:12.605 --> 05:17.587
I'm gonna get positive x squared plus x

05:17.587 --> 05:20.713
minus six is equal to zero.

05:20.713 --> 05:22.522
And we're making some good progress here.

05:22.522 --> 05:24.023
So we can factor this.

05:24.023 --> 05:25.475
And actually, let me just
do it right over here

05:25.475 --> 05:28.585
so that we can see the original problem.

05:28.585 --> 05:31.398
So, if I were to factor
this, what two numbers,

05:31.398 --> 05:33.199
their product is negative six,

05:33.199 --> 05:34.261
they're gonna have different signs

05:34.261 --> 05:35.823
since their product is negative.

05:35.823 --> 05:37.504
And they add up to one,

05:37.504 --> 05:40.316
the coefficient on the first degree term.

05:40.316 --> 05:43.626
Well, positive three
and negative two work,

05:43.626 --> 05:47.360
so I can rewrite this as x plus three

05:47.360 --> 05:50.313
times x minus two

05:50.313 --> 05:53.493
is equal to zero.

05:53.493 --> 05:54.554
Did I do that write? Yeah.

05:54.554 --> 05:56.646
Three times negative two is negative six.

05:56.646 --> 06:00.593
Three x minus two x is positive x.

06:00.593 --> 06:03.407
All right. So, I just wrote this

06:03.407 --> 06:05.798
in this quadratic in factored form.

06:05.798 --> 06:07.410
And so the way that you
get this equaling to zero

06:07.410 --> 06:09.162
is if either one of those equals zero.

06:09.162 --> 06:12.363
x plus three equals zero

06:12.363 --> 06:15.585
or x minus two is equal to zero.

06:15.585 --> 06:16.597
Well, this is going to happen

06:16.597 --> 06:18.406
if you subtract three from both sides.

06:18.406 --> 06:20.900
That's gonna happen if x
is equal to negative three

06:20.900 --> 06:23.726
or over here, if you
add two to both sides,

06:23.726 --> 06:25.942
x is equal to two.

06:25.942 --> 06:27.444
So either one of these will satisfy,

06:27.444 --> 06:28.585
but we wanna be careful.

06:28.585 --> 06:30.900
We wanna make sure that
our original equation

06:30.900 --> 06:34.143
isn't going to be undefined
for either one of these.

06:34.143 --> 06:35.755
And negative three does not make

06:35.755 --> 06:40.359
either of the denominators
equal to zero, so that's cool.

06:40.359 --> 06:41.941
And positive two does not make

06:41.941 --> 06:44.473
either of the denominators equal to zero.

06:44.473 --> 06:45.845
So it looks like we're in good shape.

06:45.845 --> 06:47.373
There's two solutions

06:47.373 --> 06:50.540
to that equation.

06:50.540 --> 06:53.613
If one of them made any of the
denominators equal to zero,

06:53.613 --> 06:56.319
